      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A 68-year-old Asian gentleman presented with limiting angina pectoris following myocardial infarction. Coronary angiography demonstrated complete occlusion of the left anterior descending artery after the first septal, the proximal right coronary artery and also the proximal part of the circumflex. The myocardial blood supply was wholly dependent on two septal arteries."},
